cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the paper it accompanies."
type: software
title: "[SOFTWARE] Real-time temperature correction for urban sensor networks"
abstract: >-
  This software accompanies the paper "Real-time temperature correction for urban sensor networks". It implements
  RegSARIMA, a corrector that immediately replaces a missing or flagged
  temperature observation of a failing station. A regression on the other stations' observations at the same hour
  gives a first estimate, which a SARIMA model then corrects for how far the station recently deviated from it.
  The directory src/models holds RegSARIMA and the models it is compared with, src/scripts the experiments of the
  paper, src/plotting the scripts that produce its figures and tables, and src/data the loading of the datasets,
  including a script that downloads the RMI observations. The README of each directory explains how to run its code.
  The RMI observations are openly available, while the TURCLIM observations and the synthetic dataset are available
  on request, so the experiments on those two networks only run when these data are provided.
